  "note": "First election of the whole Londonderry Corporation (40 members) after proportional representation was abolished, on the restored wards; nominations closed Friday 5 January 1923 (polling day would have been 15 January). The Nationalists boycotted the election and no candidates were nominated for the South and West wards; the Returning Officer gave notice that the retiring aldermen and councillors for those wards would be deemed re-elected (Derry Journal, 8 and 10 January 1923), so no South Ward contest is recorded here; the West Ward members deemed re-elected are recorded separately (gapfill-west, Nov 2026). North, East and Waterside were all filled unopposed after W. G. Webb, J.P., an official Unionist nominee for Waterside, withdrew: 22 official Unionists, one unofficial Unionist and one British Legion member according to the News-Letter (8 January 1923). The reports do not say which of each ward's members were aldermen. Alderman Alexander Anderson, J.P., an official Unionist alderman in the old Corporation, was nominated as an Independent Unionist against the official Unionist slate; the other seven were the official Unionist nominees. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected (council-audit, Nov 2026): the note no longer says West Ward is unrecorded; West Ward's deemed members are now recorded (Derry Journal, 8 January 1923, p. 6 read on the page image for the names here)."
